Camico's third quarter adjusted loss, Motley Fool Canada reports, was driven by transitory

00:01:53.115 --> 00:01:57.815
factors, and the balance sheet remains pristine enough that the increase would not have happened

00:01:57.815 --> 00:02:00.495
without visibility into upcoming free cash flow.

00:02:00.855 --> 00:02:07.655
The shares sit about 25% lower year to date, and roughly 44% below January's all-time highs,

00:02:08.155 --> 00:02:12.695
which is the kind of drawdown that makes a raised payout look either brave or reckless until

00:02:12.695 --> 00:02:13.695
you check the cash.

00:02:14.295 --> 00:02:17.475
Dividend income screening inside Registered Accounts is the method.

00:02:18.055 --> 00:02:22.735
You use yield, payout coverage, and balance sheet strength to find payers that can compound

00:02:22.735 --> 00:02:29.735
tax-free in a tax-free savings account, or TFSA, instead of buying a yield because it looks large on a

00:02:29.735 --> 00:02:37.075
quote screen. You see a name down 25% on the year and 44% under the January high. Management lifts

00:02:37.075 --> 00:02:42.255
the payout anyway, and your finger is already on the buy button. Do you take the income or do you

00:02:42.255 --> 00:02:48.515
wait until operating funds coverage clears 80%. Here is how I'd think about it. On wealth simple or

00:02:48.515 --> 00:02:53.615
quest trade, and I have no financial relationship with wealth, simple, quest trade, or interactive

00:02:53.615 --> 00:02:54.115
brokers.

00:02:54.655 --> 00:03:00.295
Sort TSX names yielding more than 4%, then open the latest quarter and keep only those

00:03:00.295 --> 00:03:05.215
where operating funds cover more than 80% of the payout, and net debt sits under two

00:03:05.215 --> 00:03:10.715
times earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation, and amortization, or EBITDA.

00:03:11.415 --> 00:03:13.755
Treat coverage the way a landlord treats a renewal.

00:03:14.375 --> 00:03:17.415
You do not extend the lease because last year's rent was attractive.

00:03:17.415 --> 00:03:22.355
You extend it because this year's paycheck still covers the rent, and a raised dividend

00:03:22.355 --> 00:03:26.235
without that coverage is a tenant promising a bigger check from a thinner wallet.

00:03:26.675 --> 00:03:32.635
The same screen helps several Canadian energy names in 2024 once commodity prices stabilized

00:03:32.635 --> 00:03:37.635
after the first sell-off, and it fails when a hike papers over structural demand erosion

00:03:37.635 --> 00:03:39.335
that later forces a cut.

00:03:39.875 --> 00:03:44.915
So you apply it quarterly, rebalance only when coverage falls under the threshold, and

00:03:44.915 --> 00:03:50.935
cap any single name at 5% of the TFSA. Data center projects are taking longer to approve,

00:03:51.455 --> 00:03:56.055
and that slower pace may clear bottlenecks and keep the nuclear fuel story intact rather

00:03:56.055 --> 00:04:00.875
than killing it, which is why management confidence in future free cash flow still matters

00:04:00.875 --> 00:04:07.293
even when the chart looks broken. Remember, coverage first, yield second. Intel Corporation

00:04:07.293 --> 00:04:14.253
ticker INTC on the NASDAQ is today's simulated weekly hold. Evaluation entry after the company

00:04:14.253 --> 00:04:19.653
signed its first outside customer for the 18A process node, following years of internal

00:04:19.653 --> 00:04:20.073
focus.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:24.173
And this is a simulated trade for learning purposes with no real money.

00:04:24.713 --> 00:04:29.253
It enters at the next session's open under the published rules, holds five sessions,

00:04:29.553 --> 00:04:33.293
and is scored against the NASDAQ composite over those same five sessions.

00:04:33.793 --> 00:04:35.253
Not against the story we like.

00:04:35.853 --> 00:04:38.673
This weekly hold does not run the dividend income screen.

00:04:39.193 --> 00:04:43.053
It uses a valuation entry with the same two-check bar that screen taught.

00:04:43.053 --> 00:04:46.313
A real catalyst and a line you will not argue with.

00:04:46.693 --> 00:04:52.193
The catalyst is that first external 18A customer, which confirms outside demand for the new

00:04:52.193 --> 00:04:52.673
process.

00:04:53.153 --> 00:04:58.153
The technical setup is price against the 50-session moving average, and volume has not

00:04:58.153 --> 00:05:02.093
yet cleared the 20-day average, so the volume filter is still dark.

00:05:02.653 --> 00:05:07.273
Confidence is medium because the catalyst is confirmed while sector rotation signals

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:09.753
stay mixed, and that grade is deliberate.

00:05:09.753 --> 00:05:16.053
it. Last week's XEI hold was also medium on yield support versus rotation, and the mixed

00:05:16.053 --> 00:05:21.433
grade was the honest one, so we are not promoting this to high on narrative alone. Tech is

00:05:21.433 --> 00:05:26.033
the sector where the rules-based record has shown positive historical alpha, and the

00:05:26.033 --> 00:05:31.733
pick stays inside that family while still enforcing valuation discipline, and a predefined technical

00:05:31.733 --> 00:05:37.273
support line. Because chasing the 18A story without the line is how a good catalyst becomes

00:05:37.273 --> 00:05:42.673
an unbounded loss. If Intel prints a daily close under the 50-session moving average,

00:05:43.253 --> 00:05:49.093
the thesis is finished before the stop is even asked to work. The stop loss sits 8% below entry

00:05:49.093 --> 00:05:56.693
and caps the simulated loss at $80 on the $1,000 position if it is hit intraday. The target band is

00:05:56.693 --> 00:06:03.693
plus 3% to plus 7% over the five-session window if customer momentum holds, and we do not move the

00:06:03.693 --> 00:06:09.892
validation because the story got more interesting midweek. We simulated buying XEI at the Thursday

00:06:09.892 --> 00:06:18.832
open at $40.65 and exited at the Wednesday close at $39.51, a full five-session horizon from

00:06:18.832 --> 00:06:27.632
Thursday's open through Wednesday's close. The position lost 2.80%, minus $28.4 on the $1,000 stake,

00:06:27.632 --> 00:06:36.272
while the NASDAQ over those same sessions fell 2.64%, so the matched window alpha was minus 0.16%.

00:06:36.272 --> 00:06:42.292
Stated confidence was medium, the stated invalidation was a daily close below the 50 session moving

00:06:42.292 --> 00:06:48.432
average, and that line never mattered. The 8% stop was not reached either. This didn't work,

00:06:48.672 --> 00:06:53.932
and the adjustment is not a tighter stop after the fact. It is respecting rotation pressure even

00:06:53.932 --> 00:06:58.332
even when yield support is doing some of the job, which is exactly what the medium grade

00:06:58.332 --> 00:06:59.832
was already trying to say.

00:07:00.212 --> 00:07:05.392
Yield support can still lag when sector rotation dominates, and a stop that never fires

00:07:05.392 --> 00:07:08.212
is not the same thing as a thesis that beat the index.

00:07:08.832 --> 00:07:13.692
The medium call fit the result, mix setup, small lag, no drama, no excuse.

