00:10:19.953 --> 00:10:26.893
of P&amp;L of plus $193.8, and the process is still learning from mixed-medium setups where

00:10:26.893 --> 00:10:33.884
rotation pressure outweighed a tidy yield. You hold XEQT as the entire TFSA, and it drops

00:10:33.884 --> 00:10:39.324
8% in a single week when global equities rotate. Do you sell the account or do you already

00:10:39.324 --> 00:10:44.384
have a sleeve you can cut without touching the foundation? Core satellite construction answers

00:10:44.384 --> 00:10:50.964
that by keeping 70% in a low-cost global equity ETF that rebalances itself across regions

00:10:50.964 --> 00:10:56.064
and sectors, then using the remaining 30% for targeted satellite positions that can

00:10:56.064 --> 00:10:57.124
be trimmed on their own.

00:10:57.824 --> 00:11:02.504
The mechanism is a house with a poured foundation and a workshop you can rearrange without jack

00:11:02.504 --> 00:11:03.484
hammering the basement.

00:11:04.124 --> 00:11:09.184
The core is the foundation, the satellites are the workshop, and an 8% week in the core

00:11:09.184 --> 00:11:13.584
hurts less when only 30% of the capital was ever allowed to concentrate on a theme.

00:11:14.364 --> 00:11:19.864
Set a 25% rebalancing band around those target weights and review it only on quarter-end

00:11:19.864 --> 00:11:24.224
statements, which stops you from trading every headline while still letting a satellite

00:11:24.224 --> 00:11:27.444
ideas outperformance get harvested when it actually appears.

00:11:28.144 --> 00:11:31.304
The misconception is that every position must be watched daily.

00:11:31.904 --> 00:11:36.664
The fix is to treat the core as set and forget and to require both a fundamental catalyst

00:11:36.664 --> 00:11:41.324
and a volume spike above the 20-day average before you add or resize any satellite.

00:11:42.068 --> 00:11:52.748
Open the brokerage, find any energy or read-holding, and check whether the latest quarterly payout is covered by at least 80% of adjusted funds from operations, or AFFO.

00:11:53.288 --> 00:11:56.928
If it is not, write the name down for possible rebalancing this week.

